# Client identity (not built yet)

People sign up for more than one program, create a second account, or use a different phone number. Do not add unique constraints on email or phone, merge-by-phone, or "one UUID per person" matching unless Matthew asks for that work.

When we design it, the usual model is one person id; email-cannot-be-the-same is a common first lock. Phone is a bad unique key here because people share phones and change numbers. Until then, multiple Client rows for one person are allowed.
